Read AGENTS.md and resources/media-digest.md. Follow its daily-item rules. Tool gate, before anything else: check that Git and web access to the item's source answer. If any fails, stop and do none of the run. Name each failing tool with its error and the step that fixes it, and wait for me. When I reply that it's fixed, check again and run from the top. If a tool fails later in the run, stop the same way. A source page that is up but paywalled or missing a duration is not a tool failure; say so in the item. If an item is open, post one reminder without selecting another. Otherwise present the top Consume item, at most once per local day, with title, creator, link, length, reason, an evidence-labelled summary, what to expect, and a likely/unlikely Chrome listening flag. Include searchable title and creator for finding it on the phone. Update only Today's item after rereading and checking for concurrent changes, then commit that edit on its own. If the queue is empty, suggest a sweep in one line.
